WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
21 July 1983.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:09.510
At Vostok, Antarctica, the air
falls to minus 89.2 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.710
It is the lowest air temperature
ever recorded at a weather station.

4
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.210
Ice sheets cover most of Antarctica.

5
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.270
Yet Antarctica counts as a desert,
alongside the Sahara and the Atacama.

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.230
How can a continent of ice be a desert?

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.110
Is it simply too cold
for anything to live?

8
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll map the
world's extreme environments,

9
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.710
hot and cold, and read their
climates from climographs.

10
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.290
Then you'll meet a desert paradox.

11
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.390
The USGS states that more people
drown in deserts than die of thirst.

12
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.070
Your mission: explain how ice-covered
Antarctica can count as a desert.
